      "text": "To find the total surface area of the pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the square base and the area of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Area of the square base:**\nThe base of the pyramid is a square with side length 10 cm. The area \\( A_{\\text{base}} \\) of the square base is given by:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{base}} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\n2. **Area of one triangular face:**\nEach triangular face is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a height (slant height) that we need to find. The height of the triangular face is the slant height \\( l \\) of the pyramid.\n\nTo find the slant height \\( l \\), we use the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle formed by the height of the pyramid, half the base, and the slant height. The height of the pyramid is 12 cm, and half the base is \\( \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\) cm. Therefore:\n\\[\nl = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 25} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\n3. **Area of one triangular face:**\nThe area \\( A_{\\text{triangle}} \\) of one triangular face is given by:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\n4. **Total area of the four triangular faces:**\nSince there are four triangular faces, the total area \\( A_{\\text{tria}} \\) of the four triangular faces is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{tria}} = 4 \\times A_{\\text{triangle}} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\n5. **Total surface area of the pyramid:**\nThe total surface area \\( A_{\\text{total}} \\) of the pyramid is the sum of the area of the square base and the total area of the four triangular faces:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{total}} = A_{\\text{base}} + A_{\\text{tria}} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\nThus, the total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
