      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the areas of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Area of the Base**:\n   The base is a square with side length \\(10\\) cm. The area \\(A_{\\text{base}}\\) of the square base is given by:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{base}} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Area of One Triangular Face**:\n   The pyramid has a peak that is \\(12\\) cm above the center of its base. The center of the base is also the centroid of the base square. The distance from the center of the base to the midpoint of one of its sides (half the diagonal of the square) is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Diagonal of the base} = \\sqrt{10^2 + 10^2} = \\sqrt{200} = 10\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance from center to midpoint of a side} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 5\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   The slant height \\(l\\) of the triangular face can be found using the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle formed by the height of the pyramid, the distance from the center to the midpoint of a side, and the slant height:\n   \\[\n   l = \\sqrt{(5\\sqrt{2})^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{50 + 144} = \\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   The area \\(A_{\\text{triangle}}\\) of one triangular face is given by:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times \\sqrt{194} = 5\\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   Since there are four triangular faces, the total area of the four triangular faces is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{triangles}} = 4 \\times 5\\sqrt{194} = 20\\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total Surface Area**:\n   The total surface area \\(A_{\\text{total}}\\) of the pyramid is the sum of the area of the base and the areas of the four triangular faces:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{total}} = A_{\\text{base}} + A_{\\text{triangles}} = 100 + 20\\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the total surface area of the pyramid is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{100 + 20\\sqrt{194}}\n   \\]",
